WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
What is your earliest memory of Mossville growing up?

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.540
Hmm, earliest memory.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.240
Well, when I was allowed to come out the house,

4
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.380
what I saw was a building here, located right here [on the site of the Rigmaiden Center].

5
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:28.790
The building, it must have stood about over five foot off the ground with brick pillars.

6
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:37.450
And I was told that that building was the original school.

7
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:42.710
But when I came up it was used as a recreation center.

8
00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.050
[agrees]

9
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.050
And I remember us playing in it.

10
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.550
It was a big building.

11
00:00:51.550 --> 00:01:00.630
And I remember playing under the building because it was so high off the ground.

12
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:18.270
And I remember they had a chimney when they were tearing it down they had bees in it and they wanted to . . . They found out that there were a hive,

13
00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.510
a beehive in it.

14
00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:29.710
And they only person that could do . . . That could get the beehive out was an old man live in Mossville they called Pete Moss.

15
00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:36.530
He drove a wagon with horses and his wife named Caledonia.

16
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.630
They had dogs on the wagon.

17
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:46.370
And this guy, he would come around back in the days we had pigs,

18
00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:55.070
hogs, we would take our waste food and put it outside in a barrel.

19
00:01:55.070 --> 00:02:03.130
He would come around and collect the spoiled waste food and bring it . . . collect it from all the people in the neighborhood.

20
00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:07.910
They knew what they had to do and he would pick it up,

21
00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:12.870
put it on his wagon, and bring it back and feed it to his pigs.

22
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.650
So his name was Pete Moss.

23
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:26.310
And when they tore the building down . . . Well he was the one that came and got the honey . . .honeycomb from the chimney.

24
00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.710
And I remember that.

25
00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:35.670
And when they . . . after they removed . . . They did not tear the building down, they removed it.

26
00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:44.830
They moved it to the site where they built the brand new high school, Mossville High, it’s still existing.

27
00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.750
And they put the building in the back.
